{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/463315-how-to-build-mummy-s-creed","id":463315,"title":"How to build Mummy's Creed?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-31T04:49:03-07:00","id":463315,"title":"How to build Mummy's Creed?","content":"Inspired by Assassins Creed series, I'm looking for tips to build up an Arisen with assassin or spy as archetypes. Which guild, decree and cult could fit better to it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T04:58:46-07:00","id":463331,"title":"","content":"Maa-kep seems the most obvious choice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T05:11:43-07:00","id":463333,"title":"","content":"Well, from the top of my head, the Sheut decree is associated with most of the stealth and shadow related Affinities, so you're probably looking in that direction. For Guild... probably doesn't matter that much. From a mechanical point of view, Sesha-Hebsu could work quite well, but generally speaking I would lean in favour of the Maa-Kep. Maybe Su-Menent.<br /> <br /> I would recommend looking at Grip of Death (the ability to mystically silence people in a grapple is pretty nifty), By Steps Unseen, Night Creature, and Anointed Prowess as obvious ones that would help. Meanwhile, Utterances like Doom Affliction, Kiss of Apep, Torn Veil of Forgetting, and Palace Knows Its Pharaoh enable a variety of different kinds of assassin. For a straight up &quot;Sneak in, stab target, sneak out&quot; with rough parallels to the Assassins of Assassin's Creed I would probably make a Maa-Kep of the Sheut decree. Take Am-Khaibit as your Judge, giving you Night Creature as an Affinity and a purview of passing judgement upon those who perpetuate crimes against humanity. Add By Steps Unseen for the third Affinity, and pick up... let's say Torn Veil of Forgetting and Blessed is the God-King. Both are mostly just for Tier 1, Torn Veil allowing you to pass unnoticed while Blessed is the God-King lets you ensure that your killing blow seals the deal. But really, there are a whole host of powers that would work well for such a character. Mummies have quite a lot of ways to get in close and kill quietly.<br /> <br /> And any of the Deceived would probably do an even better job...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T14:07:29-07:00","id":463853,"title":"","content":"Jackal-Headed Maa-Kep sounds like your best bet.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, go really crazy with it and play a sadikh who does espionage work for their master with every awakening. A fasad works just as well if you really wanna get weird.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T01:43:01-07:00","id":465795,"title":"","content":"But in core book the Jackal-headed are depicted more like heremits than deadly killers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T03:52:14-07:00","id":467190,"title":"","content":"Specifically, they're philosophers. Of all the Decrees, they're the most likely to live by a &quot;Creed&quot;.<br /> <br /> And besides, all the stealth-related Affinities are Sheut-based. Barring some applications of Anointed Prowess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T12:16:50-07:00","id":468618,"title":"","content":"Besides, Assassins were hermits and religious recluses before they were deadly killers, whether one goes with the historical or fantastical versions. The historical versions weren't even so much deadly killers as they were incredibly effective suicidal agents, which I would consider a big difference. The fantasy assassins have exit strategies, the historical assassins have one exit strategy that isn't usually an option in a roleplaying game of any length.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T16:37:08-07:00","id":468941,"title":"","content":"But, interestingly, is (sort of) an option for an Arisen. Death Cycles aren't exactly pleasant, but they're certainly survivable if you don't do them constantly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T18:41:08-07:00","id":469043,"title":"","content":"If you want, you can even have them have coopted a Nizari Hashashin Sect. The cult thinks they're the returning Mahdi come to wipe the world of injustice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T10:27:44-07:00","id":470240,"title":"","content":"Indeed, about the cult I were thinking about an assassins sect which in modern ages evolved into a secret intelligence agency and of course they're still deadly killers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T23:44:57-07:00","id":470978,"title":"","content":"Assassin's creed in WoD?<br /> I kind of seeing it going like this: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=20QBe43tyVM\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=20QBe43tyVM</a><br /> <br /> As some of the things in AC seem a bit cheesy. However I bet this would be fun to play Altair the Mummy in a campaign.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5554-psychic_monkey","name":"Psychic_Monkey","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T02:21:46-07:00","id":471026,"title":"","content":"It's not like I want to play a mummified Altair I were just wondering how import and settle some AC elements on mummies and their cults...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}